# Enforce LF line endings on text files regardless of working-OS default.
# Reason: Windows + git-bash sessions intermittently introduce CRLF (notably
# on files created via Claude Code's Write tool from earlier sessions). Mixed
# CRLF/LF defeats grep `^---$` and similar line-anchored regexes (real bug
# surfaced 2026-04-26 when 2 lens files were CRLF and 9 were LF).
#
# `text=auto` lets Git autodetect text vs binary; `eol=lf` forces LF in the
# repo (working-tree may still be CRLF on Windows, but storage is LF).

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit per-extension rules so future binary additions don't accidentally
# get text-treated.
*.md         text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.yaml       text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.json       text eol=lf
*.py         text eol=lf
*.txt        text eol=lf
.gitignore   text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary file types — never text-process these.
*.png        binary
*.jpg        binary
*.jpeg       binary
*.gif        binary
*.pdf        binary
*.tar        binary
*.gz         binary
*.zip        binary
